{
  "file": "common childhood",
  "page": 94,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        113.12979888916016,
        27.289522171020508,
        340.4130554199219,
        35.34652328491211
      ],
      "text": "RECOMMENDATIONS FOR MANAGEMENT OF COMMON CHILDHOOD CONDITIONS",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 7.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        59.74208068847656,
        399.1527099609375,
        73.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "n = 60) and adolescent females (12–18 years, n = 12) undergoing elective procedures;",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        72.74208068847656,
        399.0727233886719,
        86.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "one trial of children with gastroenteritis and dehydration (6 months–14 years, n =",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        85.74208068847656,
        399.0728759765625,
        99.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "104); one case-control study of children treated for iatrogenic hyponatraemia (mean",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        98.74208068847656,
        399.0828552246094,
        112.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "age 7 years, n = 148); one cohort study of children undergoing scoliosis repair (6–16",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        111.74208068847656,
        399.10296630859375,
        125.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "years, n = 24); and one retrospective chart review of children undergoing craniofacial",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        124.74208068847656,
        399.1528625488281,
        138.23208618164062
      ],
      "text": "surgery (2 months–15 years, n = 56). Hypotonic solutions used in the studies ranged",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        137.74208068847656,
        198.22291564941406,
        151.23208618164062
      ],
      "text": "from 0.16–0.45% sodium chloride.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        150.74208068847656,
        399.0313720703125,
        164.23208618164062
      ],
      "text": "Only three studies reported on morbidity and mortality. Wilkinson et al [1992],",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        163.7421112060547,
        399.042724609375,
        177.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "reported seizures in 2 out of 26 patients receiving hypotonic fluids (OR 6.22; 95%",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        176.7421112060547,
        399.0629577636719,
        190.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "CI 0.29 to 135.8). Hoorn et al [2004] reported nausea and vomiting more commonly",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        189.7421112060547,
        399.1526184082031,
        203.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "in patients with hospital acquired hyponatraemia (p = 0.008) but numbers were too",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        202.7421112060547,
        280.22283935546875,
        216.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "small to evaluate these outcomes with sufficient power.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        215.7421112060547,
        399.1015319824219,
        229.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "Meta-analysis of the effect on serum sodium showed that hypotonic maintenance",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        228.7421112060547,
        399.0927734375,
        242.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "solutions significantly increased the risk of developing hyponatraemia (OR 17.22; 95%",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        241.7421112060547,
        399.04296875,
        255.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "CI 8.67 to 34.2). Mean plasma sodium in patients following hypotonic solutions was",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        254.7421112060547,
        399.0528259277344,
        268.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "significantly lower (OR -3.39 mmol/l; 95% CI -5.35 to -1.43), than those who received",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        267.7420959472656,
        399.0929260253906,
        281.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "isotonic solutions. In children receiving hypotonic solutions, the mean plasma",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        280.7420959472656,
        399.09283447265625,
        294.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "sodium decreased significantly more after fluid administration (OR -5.37 mmol/l;",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        293.7420959472656,
        399.0429382324219,
        307.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "95% CI -8.79 to -1.94). Three studies reported a decrease in plasma sodium despite",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        306.7420959472656,
        399.0726623535156,
        320.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "the infusion of isotonic or near-isotonic maintenance fluids, but none reported on the",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        319.7420959472656,
        222.75286865234375,
        333.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "risk of hypernatraemia with these fluids.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        344.2607116699219,
        163.95286560058594,
        356.2507019042969
      ],
      "text": "12.1.2\t Benefits and risks",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        359.9153747558594,
        399.1529235839844,
        373.4053955078125
      ],
      "text": "In two institutions in the UK where there were incidents of hyponatraemia due to use",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        372.9153747558594,
        399.052734375,
        386.4053955078125
      ],
      "text": "of hypotonic fluids, no further cases of iatrogenic hyponatraemia have been reported",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        385.9153747558594,
        399.10296630859375,
        399.4053955078125
      ],
      "text": "since the solution was removed from the ward stock. There is growing awareness of",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        398.9153747558594,
        399.0929870605469,
        412.4053955078125
      ],
      "text": "the dangers associated with use of hypotonic solutions and there have been various",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        411.9153747558594,
        399.1127624511719,
        425.4053955078125
      ],
      "text": "statements and changes in the national guidelines discouraging their use in children.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        424.9154052734375,
        399.0928955078125,
        438.4054260253906
      ],
      "text": "In 2003, the Royal College of Anaesthetists issued a statement advising against the use",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        437.9154052734375,
        399.0528259277344,
        451.4054260253906
      ],
      "text": "of hypotonic fluids. In 2007, the UK National Patient Safety Agency (NPSA) issued",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        450.9154052734375,
        399.0829162597656,
        464.4054260253906
      ],
      "text": "an alert advice to health-care organizations of how to minimize the risks associated",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        463.9154052734375,
        274.41290283203125,
        477.4054260253906
      ],
      "text": "with administering intravenous infusions to children.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        485.4093017578125,
        78.65290069580078,
        497.5492858886719
      ],
      "text": "Risks",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Obli",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        498.4192810058594,
        399.0829162597656,
        511.9093017578125
      ],
      "text": "All sick children are potentially at risk of hyponatraemia, especially those with",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        511.4193115234375,
        399.0729675292969,
        524.9093017578125
      ],
      "text": "pulmonary and central nervous system infections, and post operative surgical cases.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        524.4193115234375,
        399.0228271484375,
        537.9093017578125
      ],
      "text": "The use of hypotonic fluids may be harmful and cause water overload with possible",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        537.4193115234375,
        399.0728454589844,
        550.9093017578125
      ],
      "text": "severe hyponatraemia and other complications. Among children who develop",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        550.4193115234375,
        399.02288818359375,
        563.9093017578125
      ],
      "text": "symptomatic hyponatraemia, the incidence of permanent brain damage in adulthood",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        563.4193115234375,
        215.54293823242188,
        576.9093017578125
      ],
      "text": "is significantly increased [Chung 1986].",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        222.3800048828125,
        644.9403076171875,
        230.66000366210938,
        655.2992553710938
      ],
      "text": "80",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}